{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact route A head 0fb93d7457b21b438ca313e59796d2426e7de753 on builder/installed-host-roots-20261105, tree fc3474a2, for source request 071b437d under promise e2945d9a and review request e030b319. This approval covers the 36 paths at this head. It resolves required review 1a71cdd7 and follows rulings 0e593489, 56a48952 and aa761ded.\n\nScope. Main 8b063123 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The head adds eight commits over main, five of them since b0d3c165, and the branch is pushed. The commit-message check passes for all eight. Production changes are limited to packages/scope/src. No package manifest, lockfile, Wrangler file, Native definition, grant, wire type or card path changes. After gate commit db7634ee, only the note and the continuity gate manifest change.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Sites now follow the installed list. readerOf in site/host.ts checks `hostRegisterScopes(config.registerScope, env)` against the room's register for both hosts. It checks when it builds the reader, when the reader opens, after the token owner answers, and on every source access. A cached reader therefore closes when its root leaves the list. The namespace, repository-name and configuration checks are unchanged. SiteTokenReuse.acquire admits a register only when the list contains it. Its post-provider `current()` check applies the same rule again, so a root removed during a mint gets no plaintext. ScopeIndex supplies a fresh read of both settings on each call.\n- The workspace path follows the list without weakening its proof. artifactsWorkspaceOutside refuses a malformed list. workspaceRepository takes the register from the checked directory source only when the list contains it. It then reads that register's own birth and keeps the six bounded reads, the cohort pins, the outcome, the found claim and the repository checks. The workspace cache key now includes both register settings.\n- My search of packages/scope/src and apps/room for single-register comparisons finds the same remaining readers that the note lists. demo-creation.ts and register-setting.ts select the current register on purpose. archive-host-item.ts keeps one root, as ruling 56a48952 allows, and docs/deploy.md now says that a dap-grow switch needs that bridge fixed first. The celld scripts check only agreement between the self-host settings.\n- The cause of the gate 3 and gate 4 failures is a fixture defect, and the evidence shows it. The scripted GitHub provider returned a fractional expires_at. GitHubApp.mintInstallationToken rejects that format, so the mint stayed unknown and no custody row existed. The test then read a handle that was never minted. Production behaves correctly: a failed mint stays unknown. The repair changes only the test. It emits whole-second REST timestamps, starts at a subsecond clock, and now requires a confirmed mint with a string handle before any credential read. Every listed-root, unlisted-root, cache, session and one-use assertion remains.\n- The seals hold. Since b0d3c165, seven literals change: ScopeIndex, outsideOf, site/host.ts, site/token-reuse.ts, workspace-host.ts, workspace-lineage.ts and artifacts-wiring.ts. Each one belongs to a source that this head changes. Across the whole head, nine existing literals change, and host-wiring.ts and installed-registers.ts gain seals.\n- The gate passed. gate.exit reads exit 0 at db7634ee, tree a0a4e736: Node 135, Counting 56, Plain 3,943 with one skip and Native 1,111 with two skips. All phases are complete. before.json and after.json record a clean status and lockfile 5a717d43, and receipt.json shows unchanged source and no owned process left. The failed gates at 25000b56, 99d3c7f6 and a7d22d7c, and the invalid diagnostic at 771092e4, stay retained with their own labels.\n- Evidence. The note states the SHA-256 of all 14 manifests, and each one matches. Their 186 public files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, every SHA256SUMS file matches, and the